# BBSFirewall - Config Editor Trusted Hosts
#
# The web config editor is DENIED to every address that is not matched here.
# This file is the first gate; the username/password login is the second.
#
# One IP or CIDR per line. IPv4 and IPv6 are both supported. Lines starting
# with # are comments; an inline # comment after an entry is also allowed.
#
# IMPORTANT: if this file is missing or has no entries, the editor refuses
# ALL requests. Add at least one entry before enabling CONFIG_EDITOR_ENABLED.
#
# Examples:
#   203.0.113.10           a single admin workstation
#   198.51.100.0/24        an office range
#   10.0.0.0/8             a private LAN
#   2001:db8:abcd::/48     an IPv6 range
#   ::1                    localhost (IPv6)
#   127.0.0.1              localhost (IPv4)
#
# To use this file:
# 1. Copy to trustedhosts.txt
# 2. Add the IPs / ranges you will administer the firewall from
# 3. Set CONFIG_EDITOR_TRUSTEDHOSTS_PATH=./trustedhosts.txt in your .env

# 203.0.113.10
# 198.51.100.0/24
